  <h1 class="chap-title">Chapter II: Historical Evolution of the Bridges of Shehr-i-Khaas</h1>
  
  <h2 class="sec-title">2.1 The Jhelum and the Growth of Shehr-i-Khaas</h2>
  <p>
    The expansion of Srinagar on both sides of the Jhelum made reliable cross-river transit essential to daily urban function[span_56](start_span)[span_56](end_span). While passenger skiffs and boat pontoon bridges accommodated early river crossings, they could not support continuous heavy trade and were frequently disrupted by seasonal floods[span_57
